      {
        "id": 8736,
        "name": "brytehfryguy",
        "username": "brytehfryguy",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/f0a364/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-09-30T19:45:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hey folks. I always felt bad for Ambuscade. Not only does his nemesis turn of his main mechanic (NO! Stop eating my cloaking device, Haka!), but he feels very weak overall. Even his advanced mode feels easier than most other villains baseline.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Here are a few things we've done to turn him into a scary guy to run into. Some of these were suggested elsewhere, I'm just compiling them for folks to find easily. Feel free to add your own:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Traps play a new card</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Poor Ambuscade likes to set traps, but it's so time consuming. It often takes up most of his turn! Well now he preps them before he begins the hunt. Traps play the top card of the villain deck as they are set.&nbsp;</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A lot of his cards already play the next. Adding this in makes him run through a lot more cards than before. It's a good uptick in his difficulty but not a signifigant increase.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Ambuscade wins if he incaps 1 hero.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Ambuscade loves hunting things. And people. And one of his favorite parts after the hunt is taking his prize. His trophy. Once he has taken his trophy, he doesn't need to continue the hunt for their undoubtedly vengeful allies. He's got the trophy and he's won this hunt. So long suckers!</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This makes the fight against him play out very differently. Unless you have someone to redirct, someone is going to get low. And when Ambuscade is hiding, he's going to hit that low person. As you can imagine this makes him a lot more challenging. It makes you always have to keep an eye on your weakest ally. It makes the fight feel a lot different but still fits his theme very well. This combined with fast traps and advanced mode makes him feel like a real threat. Even ridiculous at some enviroments like Rook City.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Personal Cloaking Device is Indestructable until it has taken 9 damage</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Have you every tried to manipulate one of them? Just finding them is hard enough. Mostly you attack and hope it breaks.</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This isn't a big change, but it does stop some shenanigans. Tempest and Omni forcing Ambuscade to flip to his front side with the cloak out for example. But it also means he can hide out during the End of Days and other things. Not too much of a difficulty increase overall.</p>",
