        "id": 74963,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-09-30T19:57:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I agree Amby needs a bit of souping-up, and I really love the \"incap one hero for a win\" idea, but adding both that AND replacement of traps is probably overkill.&nbsp; Personally I don't really like the trap mechanic at all, it feels very gimmicky.&nbsp; (I do like the cards on a conceptual basis; besides being a transparent Kraven the Hunter ripoff, 'Cade also has the powers of Gambit!)&nbsp; And it always bugs me that you can attack his cloaking device, which is way too fragile to protect him for any length of time…him Vanishing is just a nuisance.&nbsp; Also his advanced text on cloaked side is irrelevant in many games, unless you have someone like Bunker or Scholar in the game.&nbsp; And it's very weird that he can hurt himself with Charged Attacks.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"brytehfryguy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/f0a364/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> brytehfryguy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>(NO! Stop eating my cloaking device, Haka!)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Needs more salt.</p>",
