      {
        "id": 74964,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-09-30T20:58:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I had a match where Ambuscade played well, he was fast and crazy. &nbsp;I used the traps play the top card rule and hit a ton of play top card cards. &nbsp;I hit two traps in a row at one point. &nbsp;Still won handily but the pace was actually fun and he felt way more challenging than his normal boring self.</p><p>The best I've done with him (and I might get to use it in our forum campign if things go a certain way) is giving him a dog target that has hp and the first hero damaged by him each round has to either discard or destroy a total of (H)-2 cards or lose their next turn. &nbsp;I use that and the traps play the top card rule. &nbsp;He has an incap side that puts items in play or has a chance to flip and recover. &nbsp;It sounds more complex than it is, I really enjoy the mechanic.</p><p>It gives him something that tries to stop the heroes from setting up. &nbsp;It actually doesn't make him really hard, I haven't found a way to do that other than more damage increases and playing multiple cards, and those mechanics are already used by other villains to be tough, and I don't like to ruin the unique feel of each villain.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
